sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4 and 5 (one swamp-role SSH identity); Orbit owns only its marked authorized_keys block (Nov 1 incident).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:ssh-access:converge
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: node:ssh-access:converge<br/>12 · Node id
  %%> Command:
  %%> - MCP tool `node-ssh-access-converge` with node `12`; API `POST /nodes/12/ssh-access/converge`
  %%> - syntax: `<node>`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Node only; the keys come from Orbit's records, never from the request
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - makes Node 12's managed account accept the Swamp Node's SSH identity and the operator keys recorded in Orbit
  %%> - keeps every other key in `authorized_keys` exactly as it is
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the MCP tool and the API; the `orbit` CLI has no command for it yet
  Note over GW: Validate, build the block<br/>task #5133 · Node 12
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12 is an active, managed Linux Node with stored SSH host keys
  %%> - its managed account is not `root`
  %%> - no other SSH access change runs for Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the Orbit block: the `swamp` role's public key from Node 209, then each operator key recorded in Orbit, in a stable order
  %%> - the block's digest
  %%> Reuse:
  %%> - a succeeded or running task with the same digest for Node 12 is returned instead of a new one
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5133 recorded with the full intent; no private key in it
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-ssh-access
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the block's lines and digest, and the managed account
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys
  %%> - the vault key name of Node 12's access identity, never the key itself (R3)
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  Note over SW: Read the access identity<br/>vault.get · Node 12 access key
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the identity that Node 12 already accepts from the Swamp vault
  %%> Why:
  %%> - the new Swamp identity may not be accepted yet, for example after it was replaced
  SW->>N: Write the Orbit block<br/>authorized_keys · marked block
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - replaces only the lines between `# BEGIN Orbit managed keys` and `# END Orbit managed keys`
  %%> - adds the block at the end of the file when it is missing
  %%> - writes a temporary file and renames it, keeping owner and mode `0600`; an identical block writes nothing
  %%> Never:
  %%> - removes, reorders or changes a line outside the block
  %%> - a key that also sits outside the block stays there
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - a file with broken markers, such as two BEGIN lines or no END line; then nothing is written
  %%> How:
  %%> - a tracked script through `@swamp/ssh` from 209, as the managed account
  SW->>N: Read the file back<br/>block + lines outside it
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks that the block holds exactly the intended keys
  %%> - checks that the lines outside the block equal the lines before the write
  %%> Why:
  %%> - proves that no operator key outside the block was lost
  SW->>N: Log in with Swamp identity<br/>@swamp/ssh exec · true
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - opens a new SSH session with the `swamp` role identity only, and runs `true`
  %%> Why:
  %%> - access only counts as ready when the Swamp identity really logs in
  alt login works
    N-->>SW: exit 0
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - every check passed
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record the block digest<br/>access ready · task succeeded
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's SSH access digest is the new block's digest
    %%> - task #5133 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: lines differ or denied
    %%> When:
    %%> - the markers are broken, the read-back differs, or the Swamp identity is refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the old digest<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Node 12's recorded SSH access stays as it was
    %%> - task #5133 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a written block stays; there is no rollback
    %%> - keys outside the block are never touched, so operator access stays
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again after fixing the cause; it rewrites only the block
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
